p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and February to March came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those 75 years. In 2025, November to December came in at 52% of normal on the middle of the grids, and in 2026 so far January to February came in at 41%. April to May is the wettest pair at 9.49 inches normal, and January to February is the driest at 5.96 inches. Grid 21769 had its driest year in 1963 at 61% of normal.</p>"}
